ir scorning,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¹And fools hate knowledge?¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤text·Turn you at my reproof:¦layout ‚¤textÙ+Behold, I will pour out my spirit unto you,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ$I will make known my words unto you.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ&Because I have called, and ye refused;¦layout ‚¤textÙ2I have stretched out my hand, and no man regarded;¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ)But ye have set at nought all my counsel,¦layout ‚¤text½And would none of my reproof:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ#I also will laugh at your calamity;¦layout ‚¤textÙ"I will mock when your fear cometh;¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ$When your fear cometh as desolation,¦layout ‚¤textÙ+And your destruction cometh as a whirlwind;¦layout§quote_2‚¤textÙ*When distress and anguish cometh upon you.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ4Then shall they call upon me, but I will not answer;¦layout ‚¤textÙ5They shall seek me early, but they shall not find me:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¾For that they hated knowledge,¦layout ‚¤textÙ(And did not choose the fear of the LORD:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¾They would none of my counsel:¦layout ‚¤text½They despised all my reproof.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ7Therefore shall they eat of the fruit of their own way,¦layout ‚¤textÙ%And be filled with their own devices.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ3For the turning away of the simple shall slay them,¦layout ‚¤textÙ/And the prosperity of fools shall destroy them.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse …¤book§chapter«first_verse!ªlast_verse!¦verses‘„¥verse!¯paragraph_sta